The '''Chandrilan Embassy''',<ref name="Narkina 5 Audio">{{Andor|Narkina 5 (episode)}} {{AD|Disney+}}</ref> also known as the '''Mothma household''',<ref name="This week">{{ThisWeek|1RQvg4EfDuQ|New York Comic Con Reveals, Tony Gilroy Talks Andor, and More|sw_url=video/new-york-comic-con-reveals-tony-gilroy-talks-andor-and-more}}</ref> was the permanent [[Politics|representation]] of [[Chandrila]] to the [[Galactic Empire]] on the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]]. Additionally, the embassy served as the Coruscant residence of the [[Chandrilan]] [[senator]] [[Mon Mothma]], her [[Marriage|husband]] [[Perrin Fertha]],<ref name="Aldhani" /> and their [[Reproduction|daughter]], [[Leida Mothma|Leida]].<ref name="The Axe Forgets">{{Andor|The Axe Forgets}}</ref>

The embassy was state property with [[Color|white]] walls<ref name="One Way Out">{{Andor|One Way Out}}</ref> and several small potted [[tree]]s.<ref name="Aldhani" /> Due to its status as a state-owned building with strict rules for what decor was allowed, the Mothmas had limited options for decoration, leaving the designs to remain despite being somewhat dated<ref name="One Way Out" /> by [[5 BBY]].<ref name="AndorDate">{{AndorDate|110}}</ref> The apartment also had a large dining room and a living room,<ref name="Aldhani" /> capable of hosting many guests.<ref name="Announcement" /> Several parties were hosted by Mothma and Fertha in the embassy, including dinner for the [[Unidentified governor of Hanna|governor]] of [[Hanna City]], who was an old friend of Fertha's.<ref name="Aldhani" />

{{Loc-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|And so [Luke Hull and I] were always working together. I think you can see it really clearly in places like the embassy where Mon Mothma is just a beautiful sea of creams, and ivories, and oyster tones, and it came together really nicely.|Michael Wilkinson|<ref name="Wardrobe">{{WebCite|url=https://collider.com/andor-interview-michael-wilkinson-star-wars|text='Andor's Costume Designer on Creating Cassian's Wardrobe and Returning for Season 2|author=Lovitt, Maggie|date=2022-11-14|work=[[Wikipedia:Collider (website)|''Collider'']]|archivedate=20221114190034}}</ref>}}
The Chandrilan Embassy was first pictured in the teaser trailer for the ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'' television series, which was released on [[May 26]], [[2022]].<ref name="Teaser">{{SWYouTube|j5UX1Adanis|Andor &#124; Teaser Trailer &#124; Disney+|sw_url=video/andor-teaser-trailer}}</ref> It first appeared in "[[Aldhani (episode)|Aldhani]]," the fourth episode of the series,<ref name="Aldhani" /> which aired on [[September 28]], 2022.<ref name="Airdates">{{Twitter|starwars|status/1557442379975573504|[[Star Wars]]|date=2022-8-10|quote=This is what revolution looks like. Watch #Andor, a Star Wars Original Series, streaming only on @DisneyPlus September 21.|archivedate=20220810191942}}</ref> It was first identified in the audio description of "[[Narkina 5 (episode)|Narkina 5]],"<ref name="Narkina 5 Audio" /> the eighth episode of the series,<ref name="Narkina 5">{{Andor|Narkina 5 (episode)}}</ref> which aired on [[October 26]], 2022.<ref name="Airdates" />

Scenes in the embassy were filmed in a practically built set.<ref name="Slashfilm">{{WebCite|url=https://www.slashfilm.com/1090902/heres-where-andor-actually-used-lucasfilms-stagecraft-technology-exclusive|text=Here's Where Andor Actually Used Lucasfilm's StageCraft Technology [Exclusive]|author=Meyer, Joshua|date=2022-11-09|work=[[Wikipedia:/Film|''/Film'']]|archivedate=20221109201335}}</ref> Production designer [[Luke Hull]] and costume designer [[Michael Wilkinson]] worked on the set together.<ref name="Wardrobe" /> [[Wikipedia:Visual effects|VFX]] producer [[TJ Falls]] and the crew built a specific [[Wikipedia:Light-emitting diode|LED]] screen using [[Wikipedia:StageCraft|StageCraft]] technology, and it was wrapped around the embassy.<ref name="Slashfilm" /> Wilkinson made Mothma's costume seem like part of the set.<ref name="Wardrobe" />

